          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hanoi has several well-regarded international schools. Which one is \"best\" depends on the curriculum you want, your budget and where you plan to live. These are the ones most often recommended:\n\n## Top tier (premium fees)\n\n**1. United Nations International School of Hanoi (UNIS Hanoi)**\n- **Curriculum:** The full International Baccalaureate (IB) sequence, from primary years through the IB Diploma.\n- **Location:** Ciputra, Tay Ho area.\n- **Why it stands out:** It's one of the oldest and best-known international schools in Hanoi, and many consider it the city's top school. It has a very international student body, a large campus and strong university placements.\n\n**2. British International School Hanoi (BIS Hanoi)**\n- **Curriculum:** English National Curriculum, with IGCSE exams and then A Levels.\n- **Ownership:** Part of the Nord Anglia Education group.\n- **Why it stands out:** Strong exam results, good facilities and links to the Nord Anglia global network, including programmes with MIT and Juilliard.\n\n**3. Concordia International School Hanoi**\n- **Curriculum:** American, with Advanced Placement (AP) courses, from Pre-K through Grade 12.\n- **Why it stands out:** Modern campus, small classes and a good fit for families heading toward US universities.\n\n## Other strong options\n\n**4. Hanoi International School (HIS)**\n- **Curriculum:** IB programmes, including the Diploma.\n- **Why it stands out:** A smaller, close-knit school with a long history in Hanoi, students from 30+ nationalities and somewhat lower fees than UNIS or BIS.\n\n**5. St. Paul American School Hanoi**\n- **Curriculum:** American, with AP courses, K–12.\n- **Why it stands out:** A mid-to-upper price option for families who want an American-style education.\n\n**6. Singapore International School (SIS @ Ciputra)**\n- **Curriculum:** Singapore and Cambridge.\n- **Why it stands out:** Strong in maths and science, at moderate fees.\n\n**7. Other schools worth considering:** the British Vietnamese International School (BVIS, a bilingual Nord Anglia school), the Hanoi campus of Brighton College Vietnam, and the Hanoi campus of the Australian International School.\n\n## Tips for choosing\n\n- **Curriculum:** Pick the one that matches where your child will likely go to university. IB is recognised worldwide, A Levels suit the UK, and AP suits the US.\n- **Location:** Hanoi traffic is heavy. Many expat families live in Tay Ho or Ciputra so they're close to UNIS, Concordia or SIS.\n- **Fees:** Top schools often charge about US$20,000–35,000+ a year. Ask each school about extra costs such as application fees, building levies and buses.\n- **Waitlists:** UNIS and BIS can have waitlists, especially for some grades, so apply early.\n- **Visits:** Tour the schools and ask current parents. Expat Facebook groups like \"Hanoi Massive\" are good places to get candid feedback.\n\nRankings and fees change from year to year, so check details directly with each school. I can compare a few of them more closely or focus on one curriculum if that would help."
